[worker] A **queue** is FIFO (first in, first out): items are added at the back with enqueue and removed from the front with dequeue, so they're processed in arrival order — think task scheduling or breadth-first search.
[worker] 
[worker] A **stack** is LIFO (last in, first out): items are pushed onto and popped from the same end (the top), so the newest item is handled first — think function call stacks, undo history, or depth-first search.
[worker] 
[worker] Both typically offer a peek operation to inspect the next item without removing it; the only real difference is which end you remove from.2026-09-16T08:20:40.539170Z  WARN temporalio_common::payload_limits: [TMPRL1103] Attempted to upload payloads with size that exceeded the warning limit. size=781717 limit=524288
