[worker] A **queue** is FIFO (first in, first out): items are added at the back with *enqueue* and removed from the front with *dequeue*, so elements leave in arrival order — good for scheduling, buffering, and breadth-first search.
[worker] 
[worker] A **stack** is LIFO (last in, first out): items are added and removed from the same end with *push* and *pop*, so the most recently added element leaves first — good for function call tracking, undo history, and depth-first search.
[worker] 
[worker] Example: insert A, B, C — a queue returns A first; a stack returns C first. Pick a queue when order of arrival matters, a stack when most-recent-first matters.2026-09-16T08:22:02.398777Z  WARN temporalio_common::payload_limits: [TMPRL1103] Attempted to upload payloads with size that exceeded the warning limit. size=786041 limit=524288
